        <mxCell id="n_e2" parent="flow" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=9.42;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;spacing=0;spacingLeft=6.28;spacingRight=6.28;fillColor=#f1f0ec;strokeColor=#2b2b28;strokeWidth=1.65;fontFamily=IBM Plex Sans;fontSource=https%3A%2F%2Ffonts.googleapis.com%2Fcss%3Ffamily%3DIBM%2BPlex%2BSans%3A400%2C600%2C700;fontSize=13.93;fontColor=#1d1d1b;" value="&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:1.28&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight:600;font-size:14.91px&quot;&gt;E2  Formation energies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;at each chemical-potential limit, and&lt;br&gt;the transition levels; plotted in&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:IBM Plex Mono,monospace;font-size:13.09px&quot;&gt;formation.png&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="111.41" width="290.37" x="2218.97" y="487.12" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n_e_f" parent="flow" style="rhombus;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;spacing=0;spacingLeft=0.0;spacingRight=0.0;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#2b2b28;strokeWidth=1.65;fontFamily=IBM Plex Sans;fontSource=https%3A%2F%2Ffonts.googleapis.com%2Fcss%3Ffamily%3DIBM%2BPlex%2BSans%3A400%2C600%2C700;fontSize=13.93;fontColor=#1d1d1b;" value="&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:1.28&quot;&gt;Find the Fermi level?&lt;br&gt;(&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:IBM Plex Mono,monospace;font-size:13.09px&quot;&gt;fermi_temperature&lt;/span&gt;)&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="122.43" width="219.74" x="2254.28" y="641.2" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n_e3" parent="flow" style="rhombus;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;spacing=0;spacingLeft=0.0;spacingRight=0.0;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#2b2b28;strokeWidth=1.65;fontFamily=IBM Plex Sans;fontSource=https%3A%2F%2Ffonts.googleapis.com%2Fcss%3Ffamily%3DIBM%2BPlex%2BSans%3A400%2C600%2C700;fontSize=13.93;fontColor=#1d1d1b;" value="&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:1.28&quot;&gt;E3: a level deeper&lt;br&gt;than &lt;span style=&quot;font-family:IBM Plex Mono,monospace;font-size:13.09px&quot;&gt;deep_level_margin&lt;/span&gt;,&lt;br&gt;or a C7 transition?&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="160.1" width="235.43" x="2246.43" y="826.21" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n_e_out" parent="flow" style="ellipse;aspect=fixed;fontStyle=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;spacing=0;spacingLeft=0.0;spacingRight=0.0;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#2b2b28;strokeWidth=1.65;fontFamily=IBM Plex Sans;fontSource=https%3A%2F%2Ffonts.googleapis.com%2Fcss%3Ffamily%3DIBM%2BPlex%2BSans%3A400%2C600%2C700;fontSize=16.48;fontColor=#1d1d1b;" value="F" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="47.09" width="47.09" x="2340.61" y="1028.98" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n_f_more" parent="flow" style="shape=process;size=0.0500;backgroundOutline=1;rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=9.42;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;spacing=0;spacingLeft=1.96;spacingRight=1.96;fillColor=#e3eefb;strokeColor=#2a78d6;strokeWidth=1.65;fontFamily=IBM Plex Sans;fontSource=https%3A%2F%2Ffonts.googleapis.com%2Fcss%3Ffamily%3DIBM%2BPlex%2BSans%3A400%2C600%2C700;fontSize=13.93;fontColor=#55544f;dashed=1;dashPattern=3.8 2.6;" value="&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:1.28&quot;&gt;Add more displaced&lt;br&gt;single points&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="75.72" width="188.35" x="3056.72" y="747.25" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n_f_in" parent="flow" style="ellipse;aspect=fixed;fontStyle=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;spacing=0;spacingLeft=0.0;spacingRight=0.0;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#2b2b28;strokeWidth=1.65;fontFamily=IBM Plex Sans;fontSource=https%3A%2F%2Ffonts.googleapis.com%2Fcss%3Ffamily%3DIBM%2BPlex%2BSans%3A400%2C600%2C700;fontSize=16.48;fontColor=#1d1d1b;" value="E" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="47.09" width="47.09" x="2880.14" y="243.28" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n_f1" parent="flow" style="shape=process;size=0.0324;backgroundOutline=1;rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=9.42;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;spacing=0;spacingLeft=1.96;spacingRight=1.96;fillColor=#e3eefb;strokeColor=#2a78d6;strokeWidth=1.65;fontFamily=IBM Plex Sans;fontSource=https%3A%2F%2Ffonts.googleapis.com%2Fcss%3Ffamily%3DIBM%2BPlex%2BSans%3A400%2C600%2C700;fontSize=13.93;fontColor=#55544f;dashed=1;dashPattern=3.8 2.6;" value="&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:1.28&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight:600;font-size:14.91px&quot;&gt;F1  Two geometries&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;the ground and excited states: two&lt;br&gt;charge states, or C7&#39;s ΔSCF pair&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="93.56" width="290.37" x="2758.5" y="333.04" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n_f2" parent="flow" style="shape=process;size=0.0324;backgroundOutline=1;rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=9.42;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;spacing=0;spacingLeft=1.96;spacingRight=1.96;fillColor=#e3eefb;strokeColor=#2a78d6;strokeWidth=1.65;fontFamily=IBM Plex Sans;fontSource=https%3A%2F%2Ffonts.googleapis.com%2Fcss%3Ffamily%3DIBM%2BPlex%2BSans%3A400%2C600%2C700;fontSize=13.93;fontColor=#55544f;dashed=1;dashPattern=3.8 2.6;" value="&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:1.28&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight:600;font-size:14.91px&quot;&gt;F2  Training set&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;D2&#39;s relaxation steps, plus single&lt;br&gt;points displaced around each minimum&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="93.56" width="290.37" x="2758.5" y="469.27" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n_f3" parent="flow" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=9.42;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;spacing=0;spacingLeft=6.28;spacingRight=6.28;fillColor=#e2f3e6;strokeColor=#1f8a3c;strokeWidth=1.65;fontFamily=IBM Plex Sans;fontSource=https%3A%2F%2Ffonts.googleapis.com%2Fcss%3Ffamily%3DIBM%2BPlex%2BSans%3A400%2C600%2C700;fontSize=13.93;fontColor=#55544f;dashed=1;dashPattern=3.8 2.6;" value="&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:1.28&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight:600;font-size:14.91px&quot;&gt;F3  Fine-tune MACE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;one model per state&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="75.72" width="290.37" x="2758.5" y="605.51" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n_f4" parent="flow" style="rhombus;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;spacing=0;spacingLeft=0.0;spacingRight=0.0;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#2b2b28;strokeWidth=1.65;fontFamily=IBM Plex Sans;fontSource=https%3A%2F%2Ffonts.googleapis.com%2Fcss%3Ffamily%3DIBM%2BPlex%2BSans%3A400%2C600%2C700;fontSize=13.93;fontColor=#55544f;dashed=1;dashPattern=3.8 2.6;" value="&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:1.28&quot;&gt;F4: does it reproduce&lt;br&gt;the CASTEP forces?&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="122.43" width="219.74" x="2793.82" y="723.9" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n_f5" parent="flow" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=9.42;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;spacing=0;spacingLeft=6.28;spacingRight=6.28;fillColor=#f1f0ec;strokeColor=#2b2b28;strokeWidth=1.65;fontFamily=IBM Plex Sans;fontSource=https%3A%2F%2Ffonts.googleapis.com%2Fcss%3Ffamily%3DIBM%2BPlex%2BSans%3A400%2C600%2C700;fontSize=13.93;fontColor=#55544f;dashed=1;dashPattern=3.8 2.6;" value="&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:1.28&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight:600;font-size:14.91px&quot;&gt;F5  Phonons and lineshape&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;Huang–Rhys factors, then the PL&lt;br&gt;and absorption spectra&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="93.56" width="290.37" x="2758.5" y="888.99" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n_f_end" parent="flow" style="rounded=1;arcSize=50;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;spacing=0;spacingLeft=18.36;spacingRight=18.36;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#2b2b28;strokeWidth=1.65;fontFamily=IBM Plex Sans;fontSource=https%3A%2F%2Ffonts.googleapis.com%2Fcss%3Ffamily%3DIBM%2BPlex%2BSans%3A400%2C600%2C700;fontSize=13.93;fontColor=#55544f;dashed=1;dashPattern=3.8 2.6;" value="&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:1.28&quot;&gt;End: spectra&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="61.21" width="290.37" x="2758.5" y="1025.23" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="notes" parent="0" value="Notes" />
        <mxCell id="r13" connectable="0" parent="notes" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=12.56;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fafaf8;strokeColor=#c9c7c0;strokeWidth=1.37;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="530.53" width="1579.37" x="1669.62" y="1534.24" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="m1" connectable="0" parent="notes" style="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=0;fontFamily=IBM Plex Sans;fontSource=https%3A%2F%2Ffonts.googleapis.com%2Fcss%3Ffamily%3DIBM%2BPlex%2BSans%3A400%2C600%2C700;fontSize=13.93;fontColor=#1d1d1b;spacingLeft=11.77;rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=12.56;fillColor=#fafaf8;strokeColor=#c9c7c0;strokeWidth=1.37;spacingRight=9.81;spacingTop=6.83;" value="&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:1.28&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-weight:600;font-size:14.91px;margin-bottom:3.3px&quot;&gt;The Γ-only floor (B3)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;C screens at the Γ point only, which gives a defect&#39;s levels as an isolated defect has them only when its periodic images barely overlap. A level E&lt;sub&gt;b&lt;/sub&gt; inside the gap decays as exp(−r/ξ), where (two-band model) 1/ξ² = (2m*/ħ²) E&lt;sub&gt;b&lt;/sub&gt; (1 − E&lt;sub&gt;b&lt;/sub&gt;/E&lt;sub&gt;g&lt;/sub&gt;). The screening cell keeps its images at least 4ξ apart, with&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding-left:11.77px;text-indent:-9.42px&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#55544f&quot;&gt;•&lt;/span&gt;  E&lt;sub&gt;b&lt;/sub&gt; = &lt;span style=&quot;font-family:IBM Plex Mono,monospace;font-size:13.09px&quot;&gt;deep_level_margin&lt;/span&gt;: the shallowest level that counts as deep&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding-left:11.77px;text-indent:-9.42px&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#55544f&quot;&gt;•&lt;/span&gt;  m*: the lighter of the hole and electron masses at A2.2&#39;s band edges&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding-left:11.77px;text-indent:-9.42px&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#55544f&quot;&gt;•&lt;/span&gt;  E&lt;sub&gt;g&lt;/sub&gt;: A2.2&#39;s band gap&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Set &lt;span style=&quot;font-family:IBM Plex Mono,monospace;font-size:13.09px&quot;&gt;screen_min_image&lt;/span&gt; to give the floor yourself (0: no floor).&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="193.82" width="500.3" x="590.55" y="1849.27" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="m2" connectable="0" parent="notes" style="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=0;fontFamily=IBM Plex Sans;fontSource=https%3A%2F%2Ffonts.googleapis.com%2Fcss%3Ffamily%3DIBM%2BPlex%2BSans%3A400%2C600%2C700;fontSize=13.93;fontColor=#1d1d1b;spacingLeft=11.77;rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=12.56;fillColor=#fafaf8;strokeColor=#c9c7c0;strokeWidth=1.37;spacingRight=9.81;spacingTop=6.83;" value="&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:1.28&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-weight:600;font-size:14.91px;margin-bottom:3.3px&quot;&gt;Cell sizes are image distances&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;A size is the shortest distance between a defect and its periodic images (Å), not an atom count. The sizes come from &lt;span style=&quot;font-family:IBM Plex Mono,monospace;font-size:13.09px&quot;&gt;scan_lengths&lt;/span&gt;:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding-left:11.77px;text-indent:-9.42px&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#55544f&quot;&gt;•&lt;/span&gt;  B2: MACE tests every candidate in every size&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding-left:11.77px;text-indent:-9.42px&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#55544f&quot;&gt;•&lt;/span&gt;  B3: the screening cell fits the worst case and the Γ-only floor&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding-left:11.77px;text-indent:-9.42px&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#55544f&quot;&gt;•&lt;/span&gt;  C2b: checks the screening cell with 2 × 2 × 2 k-points&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding-left:11.77px;text-indent:-9.42px&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#55544f&quot;&gt;•&lt;/span&gt;  D0: steps up the sizes to each defect&#39;s own production cell&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="140.33" width="500.3" x="590.55" y="2054.86" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="m3" connectable="0" parent="notes" style="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=0;fontFamily=IBM Plex Sans;fontSource=https%3A%2F%2Ffonts.googleapis.com%2Fcss%3Ffamily%3DIBM%2BPlex%2BSans%3A400%2C600%2C700;fontSize=13.93;fontColor=#1d1d1b;spacingLeft=11.77;rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=12.56;fillColor=#fafaf8;strokeColor=#c9c7c0;strokeWidth=1.37;spacingRight=9.81;spacingTop=6.83;" value="&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:1.28&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-weight:600;font-size:14.91px;margin-bottom:3.3px&quot;&gt;How the CASTEP jobs run&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Every CASTEP step hands its jobs to &lt;span style=&quot;font-family:IBM Plex Mono,monospace;font-size:13.09px&quot;&gt;supercell_convergence.py&lt;/span&gt;:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding-left:11.77px;text-indent:-9.42px&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#55544f&quot;&gt;•&lt;/span&gt;  one short dry run per distinct input sizes the jobs: nodes, memory, partition and walltime&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding-left:11.77px;text-indent:-9.42px&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#55544f&quot;&gt;•&lt;/span&gt;  no more than &lt;span style=&quot;font-family:IBM Plex Mono,monospace;font-size:13.09px&quot;&gt;max_jobs&lt;/span&gt; are queued at once&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding-left:11.77px;text-indent:-9.42px&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#55544f&quot;&gt;•&lt;/span&gt;  a job that runs out of time carries on from its &lt;span style=&quot;font-family:IBM Plex Mono,monospace;font-size:13.09px&quot;&gt;.check&lt;/span&gt; (up to &lt;span style=&quot;font-family:IBM Plex Mono,monospace;font-size:13.09px&quot;&gt;max_restarts&lt;/span&gt; times; screening jobs don&#39;t restart)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding-left:11.77px;text-indent:-9.42px&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#55544f&quot;&gt;•&lt;/span&gt;  with &lt;span style=&quot;font-family:IBM Plex Mono,monospace;font-size:13.09px&quot;&gt;tolerate_failures&lt;/span&gt; (screening, D0, D1), a failed job is flagged and the others carry on&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding-left:11.77px;text-indent:-9.42px&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#55544f&quot;&gt;•&lt;/span&gt;  a finished job whose inputs have since changed stops the run, so results from two different settings never mix&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding-left:11.77px;text-indent:-9.42px&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#55544f&quot;&gt;•&lt;/span&gt;  &lt;span style=&quot;font-family:IBM Plex Mono,monospace;font-size:13.09px&quot;&gt;touch &amp;lt;workdir&amp;gt;/STOP&lt;/span&gt; stops dwf.py; queued jobs keep running&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="229.49" width="500.3" x="1669.62" y="1279.19" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="m4" connectable="0" parent="notes" style="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=0;fontFamily=IBM Plex Sans;fontSource=https%3A%2F%2Ffonts.googleapis.com%2Fcss%3Ffamily%3DIBM%2BPlex%2BSans%3A400%2C600%2C700;fontSize=13.93;fontColor=#1d1d1b;spacingLeft=11.77;rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=12.56;fillColor=#fafaf8;strokeColor=#c9c7c0;strokeWidth=1.37;spacingRight=9.81;spacingTop=6.83;" value="&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:1.28&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-weight:600;font-size:14.91px;margin-bottom:3.3px&quot;&gt;Stopping and rerunning&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:IBM Plex Mono,monospace;font-size:13.09px&quot;&gt;&amp;lt;workdir&amp;gt;/state.json&lt;/span&gt; records each finished step, with a fingerprint of its settings, input files and earlier results.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding-left:11.77px;text-indent:-9.42px&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#55544f&quot;&gt;•&lt;/span&gt;  stopped (STOP, Ctrl-C, &lt;span style=&quot;font-family:IBM Plex Mono,monospace;font-size:13.09px&quot;&gt;--no-wait&lt;/span&gt;, a crash)? Run the same command again: finished steps are skipped, and jobs already submitted or finished are picked up&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding-left:11.77px;text-indent:-9.42px&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#55544f&quot;&gt;•&lt;/span&gt;  changed a setting? The steps that depend on it run again; jobs whose inputs are unchanged are reused&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding-left:11.77px;text-indent:-9.42px&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#55544f&quot;&gt;•&lt;/span&gt;  &lt;span style=&quot;font-family:IBM Plex Mono,monospace;font-size:13.09px&quot;&gt;--redo STEP&lt;/span&gt;: start that step again (its old files are kept)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding-left:11.77px;text-indent:-9.42px&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#55544f&quot;&gt;•&lt;/span&gt;  &lt;span style=&quot;font-family:IBM Plex Mono,monospace;font-size:13.09px&quot;&gt;--status&lt;/span&gt;: what has finished; &lt;span style=&quot;font-family:IBM Plex Mono,monospace;font-size:13.09px&quot;&gt;--until B&lt;/span&gt;: stop after phase B&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding-left:11.77px;text-indent:-9.42px&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#55544f&quot;&gt;•&lt;/span&gt;  &lt;span style=&quot;font-family:IBM Plex Mono,monospace;font-size:13.09px&quot;&gt;--prepare-only&lt;/span&gt;: write the job inputs, but submit nothing&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="211.66" width="500.3" x="2209.16" y="1279.19" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="m5" connectable="0" parent="notes" style="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=0;fontFamily=IBM Plex Sans;fontSource=https%3A%2F%2Ffonts.googleapis.com%2Fcss%3Ffamily%3DIBM%2BPlex%2BSans%3A400%2C600%2C700;fontSize=13.93;fontColor=#1d1d1b;spacingLeft=11.77;rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=12.56;fillColor=#fafaf8;strokeColor=#c9c7c0;strokeWidth=1.37;spacingRight=9.81;spacingTop=6.83;" value="&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:1.28&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-weight:600;font-size:14.91px;margin-bottom:3.3px&quot;&gt;Phase F is not scripted yet&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;E3 lists the defects worth a lineshape (&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:IBM Plex Mono,monospace;font-size:13.09px&quot;&gt;for_F&lt;/span&gt; in &lt;span style=&quot;font-family:IBM Plex Mono,monospace;font-size:13.09px&quot;&gt;E_thermo/results.json&lt;/span&gt;), and D2 saves the D0 and D1 relaxation steps as training data for F2. Planned tools: MACE for fine-tuning and phonons, and lineshape_tools (Turiansky et al.) for the spectra.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="122.5" width="500.3" x="2748.69" y="1279.19" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="m6" connectable="0" parent="notes" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=0;fontFamily=IBM Plex Sans;fontSource=https%3A%2F%2Ffonts.googleapis.com%2Fcss%3Ffamily%3DIBM%2BPlex%2BSans%3A400%2C600%2C700;fontSize=13.93;fontColor=#1d1d1b;spacingLeft=11.77;" value="&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:1.28&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;Every MACE step in this chart (green) is charge-blind: the model sees no charge and no spin. It only prepares structures (B2, C1) and never ranks charge states, so CASTEP does all the searching in C and D, and F needs one fine-tuned model per charge state.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;height:17.83px&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight:600&quot;&gt;A charge-aware MACE&lt;/span&gt; (Wang, Mosquera-Lois and Walsh, arXiv:2603.05238, March 2026):&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding-left:11.77px;text-indent:-9.42px&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#55544f&quot;&gt;•&lt;/span&gt;  a learnable total-charge embedding in MACE (v0.3.15): one model covers all five charge states of a Se vacancy in Sb₂Se₃&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding-left:11.77px;text-indent:-9.42px&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#55544f&quot;&gt;•&lt;/span&gt;  multi-fidelity: PBE relaxations, plus HSE06 single points on about 10 % of them&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding-left:11.77px;text-indent:-9.42px&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#55544f&quot;&gt;•&lt;/span&gt;  transition levels within 0.02 eV of HSE06; exploring the energy surface about three orders of magnitude cheaper&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding-left:11.77px;text-indent:-9.42px&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#55544f&quot;&gt;•&lt;/span&gt;  models with explicit charges (MACE-POLAR, MACE-LES) did worse there, and the molecular MACE-POLAR-1 missed the DFT ground states&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;height:17.83px&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight:600&quot;&gt;What would stay.&lt;/span&gt; CASTEP makes the training data and has the last word: gap states, spin and excited states still need it. A model trained on one defect is reliable only near the structures it has seen, so a minimum it finds far from them is a candidate to check in CASTEP, not a result.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;height:17.83px&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight:600&quot;&gt;Status.&lt;/span&gt; One preprint and one test material; its data and trained weights “will be made available upon publication”. It used VASP (PAW); with CASTEP, the PBE and hybrid runs would need the same pseudopotentials and settings.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="469.71" width="667.06" x="1669.62" y="1582.51" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="m7" connectable="0" parent="notes" style="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=0;fontFamily=IBM Plex Sans;fontSource=https%3A%2F%2Ffonts.googleapis.com%2Fcss%3Ffamily%3DIBM%2BPlex%2BSans%3A400%2C600%2C700;fontSize=13.93;fontColor=#1d1d1b;spacingLeft=11.77;rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=12.56;fillColor=#fafaf8;strokeColor=#c9c7c0;strokeWidth=1.37;spacingRight=9.81;spacingTop=6.83;" value="&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:1.28&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-weight:600;font-size:14.91px;margin-bottom:3.3px&quot;&gt;What the filters in C keep&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding-left:11.77px;text-indent:-9.42px&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#55544f&quot;&gt;•&lt;/span&gt;  C1 &lt;span style=&quot;font-family:IBM Plex Mono,monospace;font-size:13.09px&quot;&gt;configuration_margin&lt;/span&gt;: arrangements within that of the lowest MACE energy of their composition (MACE ignores the charge)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding-left:11.77px;text-indent:-9.42px&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#55544f&quot;&gt;•&lt;/span&gt;  C3 hull: an arrangement stays if, at some Fermi level in the gap, its lowest formation energy is within &lt;span style=&quot;font-family:IBM Plex Mono,monospace;font-size:13.09px&quot;&gt;hull_margin&lt;/span&gt; of its group&#39;s&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding-left:11.77px;text-indent:-9.42px&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#55544f&quot;&gt;•&lt;/span&gt;  C3 duplicates: one that relaxed into a lower one&#39;s structure goes&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding-left:11.77px;text-indent:-9.42px&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#55544f&quot;&gt;•&lt;/span&gt;  C3 properties (optional), met by a charge state stable somewhere in the gap: &lt;span style=&quot;font-family:IBM Plex Mono,monospace;font-size:13.09px&quot;&gt;require_gap_states&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&quot;font-family:IBM Plex Mono,monospace;font-size:13.09px&quot;&gt;require_spin&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&quot;font-family:IBM Plex Mono,monospace;font-size:13.09px&quot;&gt;require_bound&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding-left:11.77px;text-indent:-9.42px&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#55544f&quot;&gt;•&lt;/span&gt;  C6: the &lt;span style=&quot;font-family:IBM Plex Mono,monospace;font-size:13.09px&quot;&gt;keep_structures&lt;/span&gt; lowest structures of each charge state&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="175.99" width="500.3" x="1669.62" y="2080.47" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="m8" connectable="0" parent="notes" style="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=0;fontFamily=IBM Plex Sans;fontSource=https%3A%2F%2Ffonts.googleapis.com%2Fcss%3Ffamily%3DIBM%2BPlex%2BSans%3A400%2C600%2C700;fontSize=13.93;fontColor=#1d1d1b;spacingLeft=11.77;rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=12.56;fillColor=#fafaf8;strokeColor=#c9c7c0;strokeWidth=1.37;spacingRight=9.81;spacingTop=6.83;" value="&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:1.28&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-weight:600;font-size:14.91px;margin-bottom:3.3px&quot;&gt;C7: excited states (&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:IBM Plex Mono,monospace;font-size:14.02px&quot;&gt;excite : true&lt;/span&gt;)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding-left:11.77px;text-indent:-9.42px&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#55544f&quot;&gt;•&lt;/span&gt;  ground state: a single point at the screening settings (&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:IBM Plex Mono,monospace;font-size:13.09px&quot;&gt;metals_method : dm&lt;/span&gt;), keeping its &lt;span style=&quot;font-family:IBM Plex Mono,monospace;font-size:13.09px&quot;&gt;.check&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding-left:11.77px;text-indent:-9.42px&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#55544f&quot;&gt;•&lt;/span&gt;  excitation: the smallest step, at least &lt;span style=&quot;font-family:IBM Plex Mono,monospace;font-size:13.09px&quot;&gt;excite_min&lt;/span&gt;, from an occupied to an empty gap level in one spin channel&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding-left:11.77px;text-indent:-9.42px&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#55544f&quot;&gt;•&lt;/span&gt;  excited state: CASTEP&#39;s ΔSCF, started from that &lt;span style=&quot;font-family:IBM Plex Mono,monospace;font-size:13.09px&quot;&gt;.check&lt;/span&gt;; relaxed (&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:IBM Plex Mono,monospace;font-size:13.09px&quot;&gt;excite_relax&lt;/span&gt;) it gives the ZPL and ΔQ, else the vertical energy&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding-left:11.77px;text-indent:-9.42px&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#55544f&quot;&gt;•&lt;/span&gt;  verdict: inside &lt;span style=&quot;font-family:IBM Plex Mono,monospace;font-size:13.09px&quot;&gt;excite_window&lt;/span&gt; (pass), outside, no excitation, or unknown (its runs failed: kept, with a warning)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding-left:11.77px;text-indent:-9.42px&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#55544f&quot;&gt;•&lt;/span&gt;  native defects always go on, and skip C3&#39;s property filters&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="193.82" width="500.3" x="2209.16" y="2080.47" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="m9" connectable="0" parent="notes" style="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=0;fontFamily=IBM Plex Sans;fontSource=https%3A%2F%2Ffonts.googleapis.com%2Fcss%3Ffamily%3DIBM%2BPlex%2BSans%3A400%2C600%2C700;fontSize=13.93;fontColor=#1d1d1b;spacingLeft=11.77;rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=12.56;fillColor=#fafaf8;strokeColor=#c9c7c0;strokeWidth=1.37;spacingRight=9.81;spacingTop=6.83;" value="&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:1.28&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-weight:600;font-size:14.91px;margin-bottom:3.3px&quot;&gt;Test C7 on one defect first&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;CASTEP&#39;s ΔSCF must work on your build: test C7 first on one defect with a known ZPL (in CaO, Sb&lt;sub&gt;Ca&lt;/sub&gt;–V&lt;sub&gt;O&lt;/sub&gt; at q = −1: ADAQ gives about 0.53 eV). If its excited state won&#39;t relax, set &lt;span style=&quot;font-family:IBM Plex Mono,monospace;font-size:13.09px&quot;&gt;excite_relax : false&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="104.67" width="500.3" x="2748.69" y="2080.47" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="x24" connectable="0" parent="notes" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=nowrap;spacing=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontFamily=IBM Plex Sans;fontSource=https%3A%2F%2Ffonts.googleapis.com%2Fcss%3Ffamily%3DIBM%2BPlex%2BSans%3A400%2C600%2C700;fontSize=16.48;fontColor=#1d1d1b;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight:600&quot;&gt;Charge-aware MACE: not in the workflow yet&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="26.37" width="395.47" x="1681.39" y="1541.03" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="x25" connectable="0" parent="notes" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=nowrap;spacing=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontFamily=IBM Plex Sans;fontSource=https%3A%2F%2Ffonts.googleapis.com%2Fcss%3Ffamily%3DIBM%2BPlex%2BSans%3A400%2C600%2C700;fontSize=13.93;fontColor=#1d1d1b;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight:600&quot;&gt;Now: dwf.py&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="22.29" width="93.66" x="2532.16" y="1565.17" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="x26" connectable="0" parent="notes" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=nowrap;spacing=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontFamily=IBM Plex Sans;fontSource=https%3A%2F%2Ffonts.googleapis.com%2Fcss%3Ffamily%3DIBM%2BPlex%2BSans%3A400%2C600%2C700;fontSize=13.93;fontColor=#1d1d1b;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight:600&quot;&gt;With a charge-aware, multi-fidelity MACE&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="22.29" width="319.88" x="2846.75" y="1565.17" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
